// Course Registration System

// Core Courses
// All students must register for a minimum of 12 credits.
// Undergraduate students must select one 100-level Core course.
// Graduate students must select a 500-level Seminar.

// Prerequisites
// 'Advanced AI' requires 'Intro to AI' and 'Linear Algebra'.
// 'Statistics for Biology' and 'Statistics for Business' are mutually exclusive.

// Optional Module
// 'Robotics Lab' is an optional elective with a hard enrollment cap of 20 students.

// Thesis Defense
// Only students with 60 credits and a completed 'Dissertation Proposal' review can take the 'Thesis Defense' module.


// Constraints
// All courses listed must be offered.
// The number of credits required for each course must be non-negative.
// 'Intro to AI' and 'Linear Algebra' are mutually exclusive.
// 'Statistics for Biology' and 'Statistics for Business' are mutually exclusive.
// 'Robotics Lab' is an optional elective.
// 'Thesis Defense' is only available to students with 60 credits.
// 'Advanced AI' is a prerequisite for 'Intro to AI'.
// 'Linear Algebra' is a prerequisite for 'Statistics for Biology'.
// 'Linear Algebra' is a prerequisite for 'Statistics for Business'.
// 'Statistics for Biology' is a prerequisite for 'Statistics for Business'.
// 'Robotics Lab' is an optional elective.

// Notes
// The following constraints are enforced:
// - All students register for a minimum of 12 credits.
